WEBVTT

00:00:10.669 --> 00:00:11.330
I'm sorry.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.050
I was hung up on a phone call with the mayor,

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.410
then tests pushed my deadline,

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:17.070
but I know we said eight, so I'm...

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.230
Right on time for you.

00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:23.429
Well, I bet even you couldn't run faster in these heels.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:25.350
I wouldn't look nearly as good.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.710
What do you say we take your shoes in my sport coat

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.469
and go get a nice dinner?

00:00:30.469 --> 00:00:31.890
I smell though you're not wearing a sport coat.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.149
Show off?

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.950
Listen, why don't we get something to eat at the new place?

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.130
You mean the place that requires

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.530
reservations six months in advance?

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:45.450
That's nice thought.

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:47.469
but we'll never get a table.

00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:49.469
We'll never know unless we ask,

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:51.469
and I hope the answer is yes.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:53.469
You know what, even if we're lucky enough

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:55.469
to snag a cancellation with the VRA's

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:57.469
latest no-fund policy,

00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:58.469
we'll have to leave before dessert.

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:02.469
Listen, we can't let a citywide curfew

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:04.469
prevents from having fun with the time we do have.

00:01:04.469 --> 00:01:12.900
I promise, even if I have to run to Madrid,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.900
I'll get you churros and hot chocolate for dessert.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.900
Why don't we just go home,

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.900
skip right to the delicious donuts,

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:20.900
and we can pretend for one night.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.900
for one night that the world hasn't gone totally crazy.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.900
The government has taken a tougher stance

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.900
ever since they upgraded our status

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.900
from vigilante to terrorists.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.900
The VRA is not just raining on the heroes parade anymore.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.900
We are going to need an arc to survive this hate-filled flood.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.900
But unlike the rest of Metropolis,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.900
I haven't forgotten who the real heroes are.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.900
And there is one in particular that I would love to snuggle up with

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.900
away from the searchlights.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.900
Yeah, we should probably just go home.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:50.900
But wait a second.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.900
I think I hear a situation that needs saving.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.900
I'll be right back.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:10.039
Did you save the day?

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:12.039
I don't know yet. Look up.

00:02:12.039 --> 00:02:53.280
You don't make it easy to ask a simple question.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.280
But that's what makes you...

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.280
You.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.280
The woman I want to spend my life with.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.620
The woman that I love.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:12.500
Lois Lane.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.500
Will you marry me?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.379
Yes.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:04:39.420
It's Lois.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.420
I don't know if you've talked with Clems.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.420
but we sort of have a big update.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.420
You'd actually be one of the first to know if you pick up the phone,

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:48.420
which nobody is doing.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.420
Oh, hey, Gestapo's on the other line.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.420
Gotta go.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:57.180
Keys, coins, phone.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:06.060
I forgot to give you this. I hope it doesn't set off any alarms.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:10.100
Nothing.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.060
Coins, phone.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:55.920
Dr. Livingston, I presume.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.920
What, the Safari got sidetracked?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.920
I haven't exactly left for Africa yet.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.920
Question, Cass.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:03.920
You and Oliver.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.920
You and Oliver.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:09.920
You're busy with work, and he's really busy with work, and then there's...

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.920
Well, all those other responsibilities.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.329
As a rich playboy.

00:06:17.329 --> 00:06:19.329
Very time-consuming.

00:06:19.329 --> 00:06:23.329
So I'm guessing that between the two of you, things must get...

00:06:23.329 --> 00:06:26.329
Complicated?

00:06:26.329 --> 00:06:29.329
Lois, what exactly are we talking about?

00:06:29.329 --> 00:06:36.680
Chloe, what really happened between Clark and Lana?

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.680
She couldn't make the sacrifices he needed, could she?

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:48.389
Let's just say.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:07:06.529
I don't say Lana wasn't the one faded to be in Clark's life.

00:07:06.529 --> 00:07:08.529
I don't know how you do, Clow.

00:07:08.529 --> 00:07:19.009
It's like you can see the future.

00:07:19.009 --> 00:07:21.009
Honestly, I don't know why you people are grumbling.

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:22.009
The security's far really good.

00:07:22.009 --> 00:07:26.790
Oh my God. Lois Lane.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:32.600
Are you expecting?

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:35.600
Spread that rumor and you can expect my fist in your face.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:42.160
When I got engaged, I thought my happily ever after was all set.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.160
But every storybook romance doesn't have a fairy tale ending.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:49.160
So now I'm just married to my work, which is fine.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.160
Listen, Kat.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.160
Well, with the VRA cleaning up our streets,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.160
you don't have any heroes to write about it anymore.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.160
But that's okay, because you can use the extra time to work on your domestic side.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.160
Snick-Doodle?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.160
Am I interrupting something?

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:08.750
Just a little girl talk with the future Mrs. Clark Kent?

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.750
Well, I hope that your new responsibilities at home don't interfere with your ones here.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.290
Neither of which concern you.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:22.220
The VRA is not the only one increasing security.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:26.220
I'm reprogramming watchtower's retina scan tonight, and you're up at 9.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.220
Don't be late.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:37.000
Lois? Redness scan?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Yeah, nine.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:58.139
You know, she should be better at crossing her teeth, not her wires.

00:08:58.139 --> 00:09:01.139
So, I think anyone who commits themselves to a lifetime of Lois

00:09:01.139 --> 00:09:03.139
deserves all the moral support they can get.

00:09:03.139 --> 00:09:06.139
Seriously, there's nothing more that I would like

00:09:06.139 --> 00:09:09.139
than to be court-side, the event of the decade, but

00:09:09.139 --> 00:09:12.139
not that the government's confirmed that I blew up their facilities a couple weeks ago.

00:09:12.139 --> 00:09:14.139
Well, not everyone believes their propaganda.

00:09:14.139 --> 00:09:16.139
Clark, come on, now the whole world thinks I'm a terrorist.

00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:19.139
Alright, it's not exactly something you want on your Fortune 500 bio.

00:09:19.139 --> 00:09:22.139
or at your wedding, so.

00:09:22.139 --> 00:09:26.139
Well, that's too bad, because I was just about to invite you to be my best man.

00:09:26.139 --> 00:09:29.139
And you're the guy who stands next to me on the worst days of my life.

00:09:29.139 --> 00:09:33.279
And I want you there for the best one, too.

00:09:33.279 --> 00:09:36.279
Are you kidding? Absolutely. Thank you.

00:09:36.279 --> 00:09:40.279
All I can say is, when it comes to planning the wedding, just nod.

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:42.279
A lot.

00:09:42.279 --> 00:09:46.279
Well, you would know, right? I mean, you married Shairo, what, 100 times now?

00:09:46.279 --> 00:09:50.279
Oh, I've heard of relationships that withstand the test of time. That's remarkable.

00:09:50.279 --> 00:09:51.279
No, or not.

00:09:51.279 --> 00:09:53.279
I suppose. For you.

00:09:53.279 --> 00:09:57.549
Aw.

00:09:57.549 --> 00:10:01.549
That sounds like a proposal only Clark could pull off.

00:10:01.549 --> 00:10:07.100
It seemed to be.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.279
Hi.

00:10:10.279 --> 00:10:13.279
Even though I married Shire a hundred times,

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:20.570
I had to lose her that many as well.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:27.840
I don't usually get all warm and fuzzy, but I am sorry about Chloe.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:35.340
You're not gonna hug me now, are you?

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:37.340
No. Okay.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:41.340
I'm just saying, I understand that it's at times like these.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.340
you miss them the most.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:52.399
Well, let's hope they never have to feel that kind of loss.

00:10:52.399 --> 00:10:55.399
No relationship can avoid that possibility, but

00:10:55.399 --> 00:11:00.399
if I've learned anything in the last, oh, 3,000 years,

00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:03.399
it's that fear should never decide love.

00:11:03.399 --> 00:11:07.409
Well, said.

00:11:07.409 --> 00:11:13.100
Alright, so while there is still plenty of champagne,

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:16.100
I'd like to propose a toast to the happy couple

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:22.570
who has finally figured out what we've all known for a very long time now.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.570
The two are destined to be together.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.570
Here, here.

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:25.570
Cheers.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:26.570
Congratulations.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:27.570
He's so happy to get it.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:56.799
Good, God, sir.

00:11:56.799 --> 00:11:57.799
Huh?

00:11:57.799 --> 00:11:59.799
Hey, that's Oliver Queen, the outlaw.

00:11:59.799 --> 00:12:01.799
Hold on a second here.

00:12:01.799 --> 00:12:02.799
I'm not the bad guy.

00:12:02.799 --> 00:12:04.799
He's lying.

00:12:04.799 --> 00:12:06.799
He came at me out of nowhere.

00:12:06.799 --> 00:12:08.799
That's not how it works in our city.

00:12:08.799 --> 00:12:09.799
Not anymore!

00:12:09.799 --> 00:12:41.169
Get out of here.

00:12:41.169 --> 00:13:24.740
The sunrise from the Daily Planet Globe.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.740
Talk about making a girl feel on top of the world.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:28.740
Just because our party was over.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:32.830
didn't mean our night had to be.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.830
Hey, did you realize that was the first party

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.590
where we didn't have to hide anything from anyone?

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:40.549
I wish that us being married met we could always be that open.

00:13:40.549 --> 00:13:44.549
Part of a superhero marriage is having two lives.

00:13:44.549 --> 00:13:48.169
I signed up for that when I said yes.

00:13:48.169 --> 00:13:50.490
Which is why I'm fine if sometimes our relationship

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:54.559
has to take a back seat to your responsibilities.

00:13:54.559 --> 00:13:57.580
Lois, those responsibilities have controlled my life

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.659
way too long.

00:13:59.659 --> 00:14:03.700
And I, we, can handle both as long as we

00:14:03.759 --> 00:14:06.759
together and I promise we will.

00:14:06.759 --> 00:14:14.299
Then nothing can stop Mr. and Mrs. Kent.

00:14:14.299 --> 00:14:20.580
Lane.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:25.940
Kent, Lane.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.940
I don't know. We'll figure it out.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:32.620
I signed up for a double life.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:35.620
You signed up for news with ice cream.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.620
I'm a journalism junkie.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.620
What are you going to do?

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:40.620
I get my own spoon.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:51.600
The scenes say the fight broke out after Queen tackled an innocent man to the ground.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:55.600
According to witnesses, Queen was only deterred from further assault.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:56.600
Clerk.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:57.600
Clerk.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:04.600
man's aid. Witnesses claim all of her Queen and other vigilantes led an unprovoked attack against people attempting a citizen's arrest.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.600
Queen's disappearance has sparked a citywide manhunt.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.600
The spokeswoman for the BRA.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.600
Yes, the honeymoon's officially over.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:27.779
We should have run that photo.

00:15:27.779 --> 00:15:31.779
And we would have if you had to play judge, jury, and executioner with my article.

00:15:31.779 --> 00:15:33.779
Not executioner, editor.

00:15:33.779 --> 00:15:35.779
Your facts weren't verified and your writing is juvenile.

00:15:35.779 --> 00:15:38.779
And you're losing subscriptions while the Daily Star sells out.

00:15:38.779 --> 00:15:39.779
Face it, Tess!

00:15:39.779 --> 00:15:43.779
Face it, Tess. If you don't get with the majority agenda soon, someone's going to notice.

00:15:43.779 --> 00:15:56.470
Tess Mercer?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.470
Yes.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.779
We need a few words.

00:16:00.779 --> 00:16:03.779
Then I suggest you call my office and make an appointment.

00:16:03.779 --> 00:16:07.570
We've already cleared your schedule.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:44.379
He's not here.

00:16:44.379 --> 00:16:45.379
Let's move.

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:53.399
You need to stitch that up yourself or call a meal?

00:16:53.399 --> 00:16:55.399
You should see the other guys.

00:16:55.399 --> 00:16:58.399
I did on television. Why didn't you call me?

00:16:58.399 --> 00:17:04.859
This was my fault. I figured you could use some time alone with Lois.

00:17:04.859 --> 00:17:07.859
I told the human speed bag you'd want to know he got his bell,

00:17:07.859 --> 00:17:09.859
Oh, wait a minute.

00:17:09.859 --> 00:17:13.859
I thought you said that Slade died in the explosion.

00:17:13.859 --> 00:17:18.859
Like so many of you, I am a victim of a vigilante attack.

00:17:18.859 --> 00:17:24.859
And while I was lucky enough to survive the explosion caused by Oliver Queen,

00:17:24.859 --> 00:17:27.859
it came at a cost.

00:17:27.859 --> 00:17:31.859
Too many civilians have been left feeling unsafe in their own homes.

00:17:31.859 --> 00:17:36.859
Too many people have suffered while too few vigilantes have been brought to justice.

00:17:36.859 --> 00:17:41.859
to justice. It's time these terrorists paid for their crimes.

00:17:41.859 --> 00:17:43.859
It's time he paid for his.

00:17:43.859 --> 00:17:45.859
Yeah, well, there's only one problem.

00:17:45.859 --> 00:17:49.859
It's not just the government against us now. The people have turned on us, too.

00:17:49.859 --> 00:17:53.859
With Slade alive, we can't exist. He knows too much about us.

00:17:53.859 --> 00:17:59.460
So until Slade's been dealt with, it's got to be radio silence between us.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:04.460
We have to go underground. Our lives as we knew them are over.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:07.460
Courtney Whitmore studying abroad.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:08.460
Carter Hall on.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:10.460
sabbatical. Clark Kent?

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:16.140
Gone.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:19.140
So now we're all card-carrying members of the fugitive club.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:22.140
You have to protect the secrets we still have.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:28.279
So until it's safe, we're shutting down Lanchetower.

00:18:28.279 --> 00:19:16.200
What a beautiful ring.

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.200
Congratulations.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:21.200
Military's not big on accessories, huh?

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.200
Only if they're medals.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:26.200
About a brat like you should know that, Louis.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:33.880
Now let's talk about the extraordinary man who won her heart.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:40.349
Listen, you.

00:19:40.349 --> 00:19:44.349
Camel Crawford. My father is a four-star general.

00:19:44.349 --> 00:19:47.349
Sam Lane's not the only general who can lead an army, Lois.

00:19:47.349 --> 00:20:06.900
This is bad. High insecurity threat level. Right, bad.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:22.500
Lois, like I said, if you broke your phone during that interview, you should just expense it.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:46.319
Fine, I won't.

00:20:46.319 --> 00:20:50.619
Hope you got your story straight.

00:20:50.619 --> 00:20:52.619
An unusually erratic schedule.

00:20:52.619 --> 00:20:54.619
Surprisingly short hours.

00:20:54.619 --> 00:20:59.619
How is it that you afforded such enviable flexibility?

00:20:59.619 --> 00:21:00.619
Well.

00:21:00.619 --> 00:21:05.619
I'm a very valued member of the staff, and my work is not confined to the emergency room.

00:21:05.619 --> 00:21:07.619
Or the hospital.

00:21:07.619 --> 00:21:08.619
So where else do you work?

00:21:08.619 --> 00:21:12.619
I'm sure that you've driven through some of our lower-income neighborhoods,

00:21:12.619 --> 00:21:16.619
or been made aware of the number of households that lack adequate health care.

00:21:16.619 --> 00:21:21.619
So are you trying to tell me that all those missing hours were spent at free clinics helping the poor?

00:21:21.619 --> 00:21:25.619
I made enough to help those in need, no matter who they are.

00:21:25.619 --> 00:21:29.619
Be they penniless or rich as Oliver Queen.

00:21:29.619 --> 00:21:31.619
Oliver Queen.

00:21:31.619 --> 00:21:33.619
According to numerous financial records,

00:21:33.619 --> 00:21:35.619
you've been on his payroll for years.

00:21:35.619 --> 00:21:39.619
If you're trying to imply that I'm involved with these terrorist activities

00:21:39.619 --> 00:21:41.619
because of Oliver Queen's funding?

00:21:41.619 --> 00:21:43.619
Hey, you're a man of science, Dr. Hamilton.

00:21:43.619 --> 00:21:46.619
You value truth, so I'm going to be truthful.

00:21:46.619 --> 00:21:49.619
Oliver Queen is relatively unimportant.

00:21:49.619 --> 00:21:53.619
The only assets of his that we're interested in are his friends.

00:21:53.619 --> 00:21:58.019
What are their names?

00:21:58.019 --> 00:22:00.019
They're real ones.

00:22:00.019 --> 00:22:09.539
You've certainly been making a name for yourself,

00:22:09.539 --> 00:22:11.140
in the news world, Lois?

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.440
Well, women's lib got me pants and a fair wage.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:15.240
I figured I make the most of it.

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:18.079
Well, I hope your fiance is not the jealous type.

00:22:18.079 --> 00:22:21.339
Considering your close relationship with the blur.

00:22:21.339 --> 00:22:23.220
I wouldn't call the relationship between two people

00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:24.359
who never speak close.

00:22:24.359 --> 00:22:26.359
I'd call it non-existent.

00:22:26.359 --> 00:22:28.980
All those articles have your name in the byline.

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:32.720
They're all about the blur, and they all have quotes.

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:39.609
You want to revise your claim that you never speak?

00:22:39.609 --> 00:22:42.670
Or maybe we should just consider all of that chat.

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:43.650
Pillow talk.

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:48.200
I want the blur, Lois.

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:53.200
You're not leaving this room until I have Clark Kent.

00:22:53.200 --> 00:23:10.559
So much for going off the grid.

00:23:10.559 --> 00:23:13.559
Carter, what are you doing here?

00:23:13.559 --> 00:23:15.559
Probably the same thing as you.

00:23:15.559 --> 00:23:16.559
Looking for answers.

00:23:16.559 --> 00:23:19.559
Besides, I've adopted a rule over the centuries.

00:23:19.559 --> 00:23:21.559
Don't go underground until you're dead.

00:23:21.559 --> 00:23:23.559
We may not have a choice unless I can fix this.

00:23:23.559 --> 00:23:28.349
I promised Lois, she and I would be together.

00:23:28.349 --> 00:23:31.349
But what if we can't? I mean, literally.

00:23:31.349 --> 00:23:33.349
If her only relationship was with us,

00:23:33.349 --> 00:23:35.349
The blur and not Clark Kent?

00:23:35.349 --> 00:23:37.349
I'm sure what kind of marriage that'll be.

00:23:37.349 --> 00:23:40.349
Let me a second, don't tell me you think about canceling the wedding,

00:23:40.349 --> 00:23:44.349
because I got to tell you how you started working on a speech, and it's looking good.

00:23:44.349 --> 00:23:46.349
You're not supposed to be here.

00:23:46.349 --> 00:23:48.349
Well, you're not supposed to be here either.

00:23:48.349 --> 00:23:50.349
All right, so I guess that makes three of us.

00:23:50.349 --> 00:23:52.349
What are we doing? We're supposed to be heroes.

00:23:52.349 --> 00:23:54.349
We're supposed to be setting an example for the kids.

00:23:54.349 --> 00:23:56.349
We can't even follow orders.

00:23:56.349 --> 00:23:58.349
Even if we gave them.

00:23:58.349 --> 00:24:02.349
Anyway, listen, I was thinking about Slade in that Mega Market Darkness thing.

00:24:02.349 --> 00:24:03.349
Omega.

00:24:03.349 --> 00:24:04.349
Whatever.

00:24:04.349 --> 00:24:09.349
Anyway, the darkness has to be driving everything somehow, right?

00:24:09.349 --> 00:24:12.349
Because I've seen hatred before, and I've never seen anything like this.

00:24:12.349 --> 00:24:14.349
We'll live long enough and you will.

00:24:14.349 --> 00:24:17.349
I've seen this level of hatred before.

00:24:17.349 --> 00:24:22.349
Humanity's darkest hours, Spanish Inquisition, the Third Reich.

00:24:22.349 --> 00:24:24.349
You're saying the darkness has been here before?

00:24:24.349 --> 00:24:26.349
Several times.

00:24:26.349 --> 00:24:29.349
But every time it looked like the world would be consumed by hatred and darkness,

00:24:29.349 --> 00:24:31.349
another force arose.

00:24:31.349 --> 00:24:32.349
Much brighter one.

00:24:32.349 --> 00:24:36.349
brighter one to send the darkness back.

00:24:36.349 --> 00:24:40.500
And you had something to do with that?

00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:42.500
Well, this time it's us.

00:24:42.500 --> 00:24:44.500
And we need to start by stopping sleep.

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:46.500
That's easier said than done.

00:24:46.500 --> 00:24:50.500
Justice isn't only blind right now. It's broken.

00:24:50.500 --> 00:24:56.000
There's no way the authorities will keep that dog in a cage.

00:24:56.000 --> 00:25:00.000
Maybe they won't, but I might have a place to put them until we can make things right.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.000
A place where he can't hurt anybody.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.339
If you think you know the blur and the other vigilantes, then where aren't their faces

00:25:07.339 --> 00:25:08.339
all over the news.

00:25:08.339 --> 00:25:12.339
A general's daughter, and she doesn't know the first thing about strategy.

00:25:12.339 --> 00:25:15.339
Right now, public opinions in our favor, Lois.

00:25:15.339 --> 00:25:20.339
Yes. But if you start targeting civilians without proof,

00:25:20.339 --> 00:25:23.339
then you're not going to be seen as the good guys anymore.

00:25:23.339 --> 00:25:26.339
I think what the public needs is some truth.

00:25:26.339 --> 00:25:28.339
Front page style.

00:25:28.339 --> 00:25:34.339
If you don't cooperate, you won't have the chance to write that or any other article ever again.

00:25:34.339 --> 00:25:55.990
You could he stare at me in my office?

00:25:55.990 --> 00:25:58.990
I realize this room's a little cozy.

00:25:58.990 --> 00:26:00.990
You're trying to make me uncomfortable.

00:26:00.990 --> 00:26:04.690
Why don't we just cut to the chase?

00:26:04.690 --> 00:26:07.690
Yes, I share letterhead with Oliver Queen.

00:26:07.690 --> 00:26:09.690
No, I don't know where he is.

00:26:09.690 --> 00:26:12.690
You see, I work and he plays.

00:26:12.690 --> 00:26:19.019
And once upon a time he played with you.

00:26:19.019 --> 00:26:22.019
Former lovers, now business partners,

00:26:22.019 --> 00:26:25.019
I'm willing to bet you share more than a portfolio.

00:26:25.019 --> 00:26:27.019
I'm so sorry to disappoint you.

00:26:27.019 --> 00:26:29.019
But for years, our conversations have been limited to this.

00:26:29.019 --> 00:26:32.019
have been limited to the matters that affect our investors.

00:26:32.019 --> 00:26:34.019
You're a good liar.

00:26:34.019 --> 00:26:36.019
But I've been watching.

00:26:36.019 --> 00:26:39.019
And I've issued enough no comments to know when one really means

00:26:39.019 --> 00:26:41.019
I'm not telling.

00:26:41.019 --> 00:26:46.769
So where are the vigilantes?

00:26:46.769 --> 00:26:54.049
Useful.

00:26:54.049 --> 00:26:56.049
An untapped phone.

00:26:56.049 --> 00:27:00.579
Instead of ninja smoke bomb.

00:27:00.579 --> 00:27:05.190
Wait.

00:27:05.190 --> 00:27:20.829
I've got to get the name of her custom closet guy.

00:27:20.829 --> 00:27:28.910
Just a slide.

00:27:28.910 --> 00:27:43.259
You love slides, Lois.

00:27:43.259 --> 00:27:44.259
Lois?

00:27:44.259 --> 00:27:46.670
I thought you were still.

00:27:46.670 --> 00:27:49.670
Be in question by Trotter and her goose-depping goons?

00:27:49.670 --> 00:27:50.670
Nope.

00:27:50.670 --> 00:27:52.670
Cleared of all charges.

00:27:52.670 --> 00:27:54.670
So I thought I'd get back to work, as you know Tess,

00:27:54.670 --> 00:27:58.670
and her inquisition is no reason to give up on a deadline roll.

00:27:58.670 --> 00:28:00.670
That's not in the employee handbook.

00:28:00.670 --> 00:28:02.670
And I've read a cover to cover.

00:28:02.670 --> 00:28:03.670
You escaped.

00:28:03.670 --> 00:28:06.670
And you totally ratted us out to Trotter, didn't you?

00:28:06.670 --> 00:28:07.670
That's what I call doing my civic duty.

00:28:07.670 --> 00:28:09.670
Just like marching you back to the authorities will be.

00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:11.670
No, you are not.

00:28:11.670 --> 00:28:15.670
I need to find Tess and Emile, and then I need to get out of here.

00:28:15.670 --> 00:28:16.670
Please, Kat.

00:28:16.670 --> 00:28:18.670
We have to put the spire out, not fuel it.

00:28:18.670 --> 00:28:22.670
The people that the government is targeting, they are not villains.

00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:26.670
They are honest-to-god heroes, and they're putting their lives on the line to protect us.

00:28:26.670 --> 00:28:29.670
Look, I know I don't say this.

00:28:29.670 --> 00:28:31.670
Ever.

00:28:31.670 --> 00:28:34.670
But you are a good reporter, and that means that your instincts are solid.

00:28:34.670 --> 00:28:36.670
My instincts are telling me to turn you in.

00:28:36.670 --> 00:28:38.670
No, Kevin, this isn't about me.

00:28:38.670 --> 00:28:40.670
Or even you.

00:28:40.670 --> 00:28:43.670
Think about your son. What kind of hero do you want him to believe in?

00:28:43.670 --> 00:28:46.650
The kind that destroys others in the name of good or the kind that's

00:28:46.670 --> 00:28:48.670
saves them and lives up to the name.

00:28:48.670 --> 00:28:53.670
You're asking me to change everything I believe about the world.

00:28:53.670 --> 00:28:56.670
Or rethink who you call a hero.

00:28:56.670 --> 00:29:01.670
But what if I told you that the blur has saved you at least twice without you even knowing it?

00:29:01.670 --> 00:29:03.670
I know you love your son.

00:29:03.670 --> 00:29:06.670
And the only reason that he still has a mother

00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:09.670
is because the man she says is a bad guy

00:29:09.670 --> 00:29:11.670
actually saved her life.

00:29:11.670 --> 00:29:22.539
Lois Lane. Have you seen her?

00:29:25.970 --> 00:29:26.970
No. Sergeant Garcia.

00:29:26.970 --> 00:29:39.130
Sergeant Garcia, but if I do, I'll let you know right away.

00:29:39.130 --> 00:29:41.130
Thank you for that.

00:29:41.130 --> 00:29:52.230
Wait. Maybe everything's not as black and white as I thought.

00:29:52.230 --> 00:29:55.230
I ever heard Trotter say Slade's found a new way to take care of the vigil...

00:29:55.230 --> 00:29:58.579
The heroes.

00:29:58.579 --> 00:30:01.579
And now that Oliver Queen's been found guilty of terrorism,

00:30:01.579 --> 00:30:03.579
they're going to use him to track down the others.

00:30:03.579 --> 00:30:10.160
Who knows what they'll find if they dig even deeper?

00:30:10.160 --> 00:30:13.160
I'll tell you what, if you're going to make your move, Clark,

00:30:13.160 --> 00:30:23.900
you might want to make it quick because Slade already has...

00:30:23.900 --> 00:30:24.900
Operation Icarus.

00:30:24.900 --> 00:30:28.900
The Icarus myth is about fallen heroes who reach too far.

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:30.900
It's the only file here flag for encryption.

00:30:30.900 --> 00:30:33.900
It's a blacklist of known and suspected vigilantes

00:30:33.900 --> 00:30:37.900
and vigilante supporters to be brought in for questioning.

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:43.900
Tess, Lois, and Emil are Slade's top draft choices for this season of interrogation.

00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:46.900
They're uploading video files every two hours.

00:30:46.900 --> 00:30:55.089
Clark, you're not going to like the latest ones. Come here.

00:30:55.089 --> 00:30:56.089
It's a daily planet.

00:30:56.089 --> 00:31:05.869
They're using our own security systems against us.

00:31:05.869 --> 00:31:06.869
Miss my typewriter.

00:31:06.869 --> 00:31:10.279
You missed a telegraph.

00:31:10.279 --> 00:31:12.279
Get away, A-Trac.

00:31:12.279 --> 00:31:15.279
Look, if Slade got clearance to access the Daily Planet cameras,

00:31:15.279 --> 00:31:20.130
he's probably using other cameras across the city.

00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:22.130
Look at this, try all the cameras across the city.

00:31:22.130 --> 00:31:26.130
Big Brother Slade's sitting a little too close to home for me.

00:31:26.130 --> 00:31:41.380
It's my office.

00:31:41.380 --> 00:31:43.380
Shepard, why don't I see Lane back in your custody?

00:31:43.380 --> 00:31:47.380
Ma'am, we're still searching the building in the surrounding areas.

00:31:47.380 --> 00:31:50.380
Take them to the secure location?

00:31:50.380 --> 00:31:55.420
Yes, ma'am.

00:31:55.420 --> 00:31:57.420
You don't want to parade us through the lobby, or just?

00:31:57.420 --> 00:31:59.420
kidnapping make for bad press.

00:31:59.420 --> 00:32:00.420
Shut up.

00:32:00.420 --> 00:32:04.329
Where's Lois?

00:32:04.329 --> 00:32:06.329
Where is she?

00:32:06.329 --> 00:32:34.990
See, when you do the final on a building,

00:32:34.990 --> 00:32:38.529
you never know what you're gonna find.

00:32:38.529 --> 00:32:40.529
Lois Lane.

00:32:40.529 --> 00:32:42.529
Where's Clark Kent?

00:32:42.529 --> 00:32:45.529
I don't know. Besides, you're way off target if you think he's...

00:32:45.529 --> 00:32:47.529
Try again.

00:32:47.529 --> 00:32:48.529
Do I Do?

00:32:48.529 --> 00:32:52.529
When are you going to accept that you can't beat the real American heroes?

00:32:52.529 --> 00:32:55.529
Last time you tried, you went down with the ship.

00:32:55.529 --> 00:32:58.099
I failed to take out...

00:32:58.099 --> 00:33:00.099
I failed to take out my target.

00:33:00.099 --> 00:33:04.099
Luckily, Fate and Uncle Sam's advanced military attack

00:33:04.099 --> 00:33:06.099
gave me a second chance to do it.

00:33:06.099 --> 00:33:09.099
Family takes care of itself.

00:33:09.099 --> 00:33:13.099
And for better or for worse, I am standing by the blur.

00:33:13.099 --> 00:33:17.099
But he's not here to stand between you and a bullet.

00:33:17.099 --> 00:33:20.099
No. No, no wait.

00:33:20.099 --> 00:33:23.369
Do you win?

00:33:23.369 --> 00:33:26.369
That's my girl.

00:33:26.369 --> 00:33:28.369
I'm not your girl. I'm his.

00:33:28.369 --> 00:33:35.369
Wrong answer.

00:33:35.369 --> 00:35:37.639
Let your friends take the fall.

00:35:37.639 --> 00:35:39.639
I heard the explosion.

00:35:39.639 --> 00:35:41.639
You were in it. How did you?

00:35:41.639 --> 00:35:42.639
Survive?

00:35:42.639 --> 00:35:49.639
Let's just say the Reaper can swing his sickle at me, but I'm beyond death strong now.

00:35:49.639 --> 00:35:50.639
Where's Lois?

00:35:50.639 --> 00:35:53.639
Your problem is you think other people define your life,

00:35:53.639 --> 00:35:55.639
but the truth is they just get in the way.

00:35:55.639 --> 00:35:56.639
Get in the way.

00:35:56.639 --> 00:35:58.639
You don't believe that.

00:35:58.639 --> 00:36:00.639
I know you had a family before.

00:36:00.639 --> 00:36:05.639
A soldier can fight for others, but he cannot afford to love them.

00:36:05.639 --> 00:36:07.639
You and I don't need to fight, Clark.

00:36:07.639 --> 00:36:10.639
Let them go. Come and join me.

00:36:10.639 --> 00:36:13.639
We can put all this to an end.

00:36:13.639 --> 00:36:20.480
You know, when I named this Operation Icarus,

00:36:20.480 --> 00:36:25.480
it was because I believe that your fall would ultimately come

00:36:25.480 --> 00:36:28.480
from your faith in your own invincibility

00:36:28.480 --> 00:36:31.780
to actually.

00:36:31.780 --> 00:36:35.019
We see a man with burning wings.

00:36:35.780 --> 00:36:36.780
Plummit from the sky.

00:36:37.780 --> 00:36:43.130
God, I do enjoy the irony.

00:36:43.130 --> 00:36:44.130
What did you do?

00:36:44.130 --> 00:36:50.090
Dead.

00:36:50.090 --> 00:36:52.849
You're mine.

00:36:52.849 --> 00:36:57.849
No, I'm not, because a true soldier does whatever it takes to finish the mission.

00:36:57.849 --> 00:36:59.849
I didn't consider this.

00:36:59.849 --> 00:37:00.849
Finished.

00:37:00.849 --> 00:37:23.289
Carter.

00:37:23.289 --> 00:37:34.179
I have something for you.

00:37:34.179 --> 00:37:43.659
Lois.

00:37:43.659 --> 00:37:47.199
What happened?

00:37:47.199 --> 00:37:49.199
You okay?

00:37:49.199 --> 00:37:50.199
Yeah.

00:37:50.199 --> 00:37:58.670
I'll get your help, okay?

00:37:58.670 --> 00:37:59.670
No.

00:37:59.670 --> 00:38:00.670
It's too late.

00:38:00.670 --> 00:38:06.059
A pro of dying, remember?

00:38:06.059 --> 00:38:10.530
I should have been there, Clark.

00:38:10.530 --> 00:38:11.530
I'm sorry.

00:38:11.530 --> 00:38:15.059
Can't always be you, Clark.

00:38:15.059 --> 00:38:26.630
This is all of our fight.

00:38:26.630 --> 00:38:27.630
Is what we do.

00:38:27.630 --> 00:38:35.019
And my passing means I'll be with Shire again.

00:38:37.550 --> 00:38:49.030
I owe you so much. I don't know how to begin to thank you.

00:38:49.030 --> 00:38:50.030
You just did.

00:38:50.030 --> 00:39:01.059
Because there has to be a balance, Clark.

00:39:01.059 --> 00:39:04.059
We can't do what we have to do.

00:39:04.059 --> 00:39:05.039
If there's an emptiness in the

00:39:05.059 --> 00:39:09.300
our heart.

00:39:09.300 --> 00:39:10.300
Remember that?

00:39:10.300 --> 00:39:12.300
I will, I promise.

00:39:12.300 --> 00:39:16.730
Oh, I am sorry.

00:39:16.730 --> 00:39:18.730
I won't be there to help you fight the darkness.

00:39:18.730 --> 00:39:26.900
But you have all the help you need.

00:39:26.900 --> 00:39:35.170
Carter.

